<p>In the latest turn in the U.S.-Israeli war with Iran, the Pentagon said the United States carried out its heaviest strikes of the conflict. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said the campaign aims to eliminate Iran’s ability to obtain nuclear weapons “forever”. Israel and the U.S. kept trading air attacks with Iranian forces across the region, while Iran showed no sign of surrender, according to multiple reports. The fallout is spreading beyond the battlefield. Reports said the Strait of Hormuz is effectively closed, a development that is rattling global shipping and energy markets. U.S. officials also said their strikes hit sea-mine-related targets tied to Iranian threats in the strait, underscoring how central maritime security has become alongside the air campaign.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Hmfmixi8Q1kaxeizikoNMFVKYeTXiN5BismaIsSG95tzKtrg_EGtb8Zl922NxTonV6MM5ReZL1opYaVxsgq2r3ZofHwCCfzVF0VdKsf3sPTO5x6XYWvputTesSerU6e8mkn6E646yHiMkvjRNVes8ERXu9Ch01F2GSOEtUXxHEEDoVfiEPAvhfv-rjYdKSZ6_rdSuYReaId3eA' alt='A billboard in Tehran’s Valiasr Square shows Iran’s supreme leaders, amid the conflict.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Missile pace: Hegseth said Iran fired the fewest missiles in the past 24 hours so far in the fighting, even as the U.S. signaled heavier strikes ahead.</li><li>Nuclear fuel sites: U.S. officials said the campaign has destroyed most of Iran’s ability to produce nuclear fuel, and cast that as a key marker of progress.</li><li>War duration: NPR described the conflict as 11 days of fighting, with the escalation continuing into Tuesday’s strikes.</li><li>War costs: CBS said early financial costs from the war’s first days are coming into view, as officials and analysts debate the scale of the operation.</li><li>Escalation signals: Semafor reported that Trump threatened further escalation, even as the U.S. defense chief laid out plans for intensified strikes.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Defense Department: Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said Iran fired its lowest number of missiles so far over the past 24 hours, even as the U.S. geared up for what he called the war’s “most intense” day of strikes. He also reiterated the goal of ending Iran’s ability to obtain nuclear weapons “forever.” (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-hegseth-says-tuesday-will-be-most-intense-day-of-strikes-on-iran'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>President Trump: President Trump said the conflict could “end soon,” a note of optimism that contrasted with the Pentagon’s description of an intensifying strike campaign. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-tuesday-to-be-most-intense-day-of-us-strikes/live-76284477'>DW</a>)</li><li>Iranian authorities: Iran’s government warned that its security forces had “fingers on the trigger” to confront any renewed anti-government protests, as it clamps down on dissent during the war. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/combatants-mideast-war-trade-more-air-strikes-iran-clamps-down-dissent'>Al-Monitor (Reuters)</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/10/world/middleeast/us-iran-war-strikes-pentagon.html'>U.S. Showers Iran With Bombs in Most Intense Strikes of the War, Pentagon Says</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/combatants-mideast-war-trade-more-air-strikes-iran-clamps-down-dissent'>Combatants in Mideast war trade more air strikes as Iran clamps down on dissent</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/us-israel-unleash-heaviest-day-of-strikes-on-iran/'>US, Israel unleash heaviest day of strikes on Iran</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-tuesday-to-be-most-intense-day-of-us-strikes/live-76284477'>Iran war: Tuesday to be &#x27;most intense day&#x27; of US strikes</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/as-iran-shows-no-signs-of-surrender-u-s-launches-most-intense-day-of-strikes'>A